  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "An ERC1400 Token is an Ethereum-based security token standard that extends the ERC20 interface with partitioned token tranches, forced transfer capabilities, controller-initiated operations, and on-chain document management, enabling issuers to represent regulated financial securities on a public or permissioned blockchain. The standard enforces transfer restrictions through a canTransfer validation hook that integrates with off-chain compliance logic \u2014 such as AML/KYC whitelists and jurisdictional eligibility rules \u2014 returning standardised EIP-1066 status codes rather than simple booleans. ERC1400 is positioned as an umbrella framework composing interoperability sub-standards (ERC1410 for partitions, ERC1594 for transfers, ERC1643 for documents, ERC1644 for controller operations), making it suitable for tokenising equities, bonds, real estate, and fund units subject to securities law.",
